<title>USA: USDA says $27 mln to certain producers in '95 ARP.</title>
<headline>USDA says $27 mln to certain producers in '95 ARP.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday corn and sorghum producers who used the 0-85/92 provisions of the 1995 commodity acreage reduction program (ARP) will get about $27 million in final 1995 crop deficiency payments.</p>
<p>USDA said corn producers will receive about $20 and that sorghum producers will be paid about $6.5 million.</p>
</text>
